.SH NAME
lean-context-apply - Apply a context — write all mapped files


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlean context apply [name] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolve and write every source → target mapping in the context.

.PP
For sources that look like env profiles (.env.*), inheritance is resolved
before writing. Other files are copied as-is.

.PP
A backup of the current .env is taken when .env is among the targets.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for apply


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlean-context(1)\fP


